Round 1:

❓ **Q1** - **What counts as "arrived"**: The glossary has **Dispatch** (the Order leaves the warehouse) but no term for arrival. A Return needs a clear starting point. Options: (a) the carrier confirms delivery, (b) the customer marks it as received, (c) a fixed number of days after Dispatch.

➡️ (a) Add a term **Delivery**: the moment the carrier confirms a Line Item reached the customer. A Return is only possible after Delivery.

---

❓ **Q2** - **Quantity within a Line Item**: A Line Item is "one product and its quantity," so someone might order 3 of the same mug. If they send back 1 of the 3, is that a Return? Options: (a) a Return always covers the whole Line Item, every unit, (b) a Return can cover some of the units.

➡️ (b) A Return covers a chosen quantity of one Line Item, from 1 up to the full quantity. Otherwise a customer with one broken mug out of three has to send back all three. (If you'd rather keep "whole Line Item only," say so and I'll tighten the definition.)

---

❓ **Q3** - **More than one Return per Order**: Can a customer make several separate Returns from the same Order, each for a different Line Item?

➡️ Yes. Each Return covers exactly one Line Item, and an Order can have any number of Returns, one or more per Line Item, until every delivered unit is back.

---

❓ **Q4** - **Return window**: Is there a time limit after Delivery for starting a Return?

➡️ Yes: 30 days from that Line Item's Delivery. After that, no Return can be started.

---

❓ **Q5** - **When the refund happens**: Options: (a) as soon as the customer requests the Return, (b) when the warehouse receives the item, (c) after the warehouse receives and inspects it.

➡️ (b) The refund is issued when the warehouse receives the returned item. Inspection and rejection can wait for a later round if you want them.

---

❓ **Q6** - **Which products can be returned**: Are some products excluded from Returns (perishables, hygiene items, personalised goods)?

➡️ For now every product can be returned, and the model stays open to adding a "non-returnable" flag later.

---

❓ **Q7** - **Return shipping cost**: Who pays to send the item back?

➡️ The customer pays return shipping. Whether defective items are an exception can follow once Q5 is settled."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":14138,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e63adc82-d72b-4ce9-b319-86dc468ae565","uuid":"d9172139-bcc7-4125-8d16-d22610ed6611","timestamp":"2026-11-09T04:39:27.142Z","request_id":"req_011CgrjjDTCQr7XCMo6MVcct"}
