There's no code in the repo yet, so there's nothing to check these answers against. Here's round 1:

❓ **Q1** - **Partial quantity**: A Line Item is "one product and its quantity". If a customer ordered 3 of the same mug, can a Return cover just 1 of them? Or is the whole Line Item always returned together?

➡️ Yes. A Return covers any quantity from 1 up to the Line Item's quantity, and the refund is for that many units only.

---

❓ **Q2** - **Several Returns per Order**: Can one Order have several Returns, for different Line Items or for more units of the same one, made at different times?

➡️ Yes. Returns are independent of each other. The only limit is that units returned can't add up to more than units delivered.

---

❓ **Q3** - **What "arrived" means**: The glossary stops at Dispatch and has no term for arrival. Should I add **Delivery**: "the moment the carrier confirms the Order reached the customer"? Returns would only be allowed after it.

➡️ Yes. Add **Delivery** with that definition. A Return is only allowed for a Line Item whose Order has been Delivered.

---

❓ **Q4** - **Return window**: Is there a deadline after Delivery for starting a Return?

➡️ Yes, 30 days after Delivery. After that, a Return can't be started.

---

❓ **Q5** - **When the refund is paid**: Is the refund paid when the customer asks for the Return, or when the shop receives the item back?

➡️ When the shop receives the item back. No refund goes out before the goods are back.

---

❓ **Q6** - **Refund amount**: What exactly is refunded? (a) The price paid for the returned units, with any Order-level discount shared out across Line Items in proportion to their value. (b) The same plus a share of the original shipping cost. (c) The list price, ignoring discounts.

➡️ (a). Original shipping isn't refunded on a single-item Return.

---

❓ **Q7** - **Return shipping cost**: Who pays to send the item back?

➡️ The customer pays, unless the item arrived faulty or wrong. Then the shop pays. This means the customer gives a reason when starting a Return.

---

❓ **Q8** - **Refund destination**: Where does the money go?

➡️ To the original payment method only. No store credit for now.

---

❓ **Q9** - **Non-returnable products**: Are some products never returnable, for example perishables, hygiene items or personalised goods?

➡️ Yes. Each product carries a returnable / non-returnable flag, and Returns are refused for non-returnable Line Items.

---

❓ **Q10** - **Exchanges out of scope**: Does a Return only ever produce a refund, never a replacement or swap?

➡️ Yes. Exchanges are out of scope. A customer who wants a different item makes a Return and places a new Order."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":14216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":966},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bdd3cd1a-af39-4b22-96e7-f5a14c229614","uuid":"1fe37b26-630f-409f-9b97-3ae481bf93ff","timestamp":"2026-11-09T04:39:38.240Z","request_id":"req_011Cgrjjvtp23fvFZiHLKnX5"}
